.TH LUCERNAD 1 "@DATE@" "Lucerna @VERSION@" "Lucerna"
.SH NAME
lucernad \- Lucerna background service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lucernad
.RB [ \-v | \-\-verbose ]
.br
.B lucernad
.RB ( \-\-help | \-\-version )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lucernad
is the per-user service that owns the wallpaper renderers. It reads the configuration, discovers
the displays, starts and supervises one
.BR mpv (1)
process per display, restarts crashed renderers a bounded number of times, and pauses them when a
fullscreen window covers their display or the screen is locked. It is controlled over the session
D-Bus (name
.BR org.lucerna.Lucerna1 )
by
.BR lucerna (1)
and
.BR lucernactl (1).
.PP
Only one instance runs per user session; starting another prints the PID of the first and exits
with status 0. The service is normally started at login by an XDG autostart entry, which the
graphical application can switch on and off. It needs no privileges.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log at debug level.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGTERM, SIGINT
and
.B SIGHUP
stop the renderers, remove the wallpaper windows and exit cleanly.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LUCERNA_LOG, RUST_LOG
Log filter (default
.BR lucerna=info ).
.TP
.B LUCERNA_MPV
Absolute path of the mpv executable to use.
.TP
.B LUCERNA_DISPLAY_WAIT_MS
How long to wait at login for DISPLAY, the X server and the window manager (default 10000).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/lucerna/config.toml
Configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/lucerna/logs/
Bounded logs of the service and of each renderer.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lucerna/
Lock file, renderer registry and private mpv control sockets.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lucerna (1),
.BR lucernactl (1)
